From 3af3303772d980a52d6a45310d6c8767b37eb5e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 10:20:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: drop the dead "<- original" annotation on the Wi-Fi scan
 pin

Batch B item. The backlog framed this as a choice - "implement the 20->80 MHz
block substitution (metal) or delete the annotation" - but that choice should
not be made, and the reason is already in the file.

pinTarget() is an identity function on purpose. The comment above its definition
records why: the old 5 GHz branch substituted the 80 MHz block containing the
scan winner, and that is exactly what made "best" and "applied" disagree in the
field. Implementing the substitution would reintroduce a known field bug. There
is nothing to decide and no metal needed.

What was actually wrong was documentation drift in the caller. scanPin() still
carried a comment stating that pinTarget() "substitutes the 80 MHz block
CONTAINING the winner - best 44 applies as 36/80", describing behaviour removed
some time ago, and a ternary appending "<- <original chanspec>" when the pin
differed from the scanned best. Since pinTarget() returns its argument, that
condition is never true, so the suffix could never render.

Removed the dead ternary and rewrote the comment to say what the code does and
why the substitution is gone, so the next reader is not invited to "restore" it.

pinTarget() itself is kept. Its own comment says it is retained deliberately so
every caller and the guard in scanPin() stay unchanged.

No behaviour change: shown was already always equal to pin. Value-only, no dict
token, 24-language lockstep untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/www/Reaper_Wireless.asp | 15 ++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/www/Reaper_Wireless.asp b/release/src/router/www/Reaper_Wireless.asp
index c0d1773cae..f77e64b243 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/Reaper_Wireless.asp
+++ b/release/src/router/www/Reaper_Wireless.asp
@@ -653,13 +653,14 @@ function renderScan(){
 function scanPin(){
   if(!SCANBEST||!SCANBEST.chanspec||!SCANDATA) return;
   var u=SCANDATA.unit, nb=nbandOf(u), pin=pinTarget(SCANBEST.chanspec,nb);
-  /* reaper: the pin is NOT always the scanned best. On 5 GHz the sweep samples
-   * 20 MHz channels (rwifi_5g_chans, swept at bw=20) but the radio runs 80 MHz,
-   * so pinTarget() substitutes the 80 MHz block CONTAINING the winner - best 44
-   * applies as 36/80. Showing only the substituted value made this read as "it
-   * assigns a completely different channel" in the field. State the transform.
-   * Value-only, no new dict token, so the 24-language lockstep is untouched. */
-  var shown=pin+((pin!==SCANBEST.chanspec)?" \u2190 "+SCANBEST.chanspec:"");
+  /* reaper: the pin IS the scanned best - pinTarget() is deliberately an
+   * identity function (see its definition). The old 5 GHz branch substituted
+   * the 80 MHz block containing the winner, which is exactly why "best" and
+   * "applied" disagreed in the field, so it was removed. The "<- original"
+   * suffix that used to state that transform is therefore dead: pin can never
+   * differ from SCANBEST.chanspec. Value-only, no dict token, so the
+   * 24-language lockstep is untouched. */
+  var shown=pin;
   var msg=`<#RWIF_42#> `+(BANDLBL[nb]||"")+" "+shown+" (nopkt "+(+SCANBEST.nopkt).toFixed(0)+"%)";
   var res=(SCANDATA.results)||[], ck=blockKey(scanRunCs(),nb), j;
   for(j=0;j<res.length;j++) if(ck&&blockKey(res[j].chanspec,nb)===ck){
